    "text": {
     "en": "If you fold a shape and both halves match exactly, the fold line is a line of symmetry.\nFold a paper heart down the middle. The two sides fit. The middle line is the line of symmetry.\nSome shapes have many lines of symmetry. A square folded in half either way matches.\nA mirror shows the other half. Place a mirror on the line and see the whole shape.\nTry this with rangoli, leaves and letters like A and H."
    }
